Another option is the [BOLD]HLA Life Essential[BOLD], which is a basic and affordable plan. It provides essential life protection with optional add-ons and can be renewed yearly up to age 100. This is great if you’re looking for simple coverage with the ability to convert to a permanent plan later as your financial situation evolves.

If you’re interested in investment-linked plans, the [BOLD]HLA Wealth Gain Plus[BOLD] provides death coverage and account value growth based on fund performance. Similarly, the [BOLD]SMART5 Insurance[BOLD] offers a shorter premium payment term of five years with coverage for 25 years, providing death and Total Permanent Disability benefits.

For savings-focused options, the [BOLD]SMART Saver Plus Insurance[BOLD] is a 20-year endowment plan with a 5-year premium payment term. It provides guaranteed cash payments starting from the 5th year, which can be paid out, reinvested, or accumulated with interest. It also offers death and Total Permanent Disability benefits.

Lastly, the [BOLD]SMART Cash Insurance[BOLD] is a whole life plan up to age 80 with limited premium payments until age 55. It includes triennial guaranteed cash payments and comprehensive coverage for death and Total Permanent Disability.

If any of these sound appealing, let me know which one you'd like more details on, or feel free to ask for further suggestions based on your specific needs!
