[BOLD]Optional Riders[BOLD]: The plan allows you to enhance protection with various riders. Some examples include accidental death benefits, Total Permanent Disability (TPD) lump sum, critical illness coverage, cancer monthly income, and medical benefits such as overseas treatment for selected surgeries and outpatient care for dengue or Zika virus. There are also premium waiver riders in cases of critical illness or disability.

[BOLD]Premium Payment[BOLD]: Premiums are payable throughout the policy term, with flexible payment modes (monthly, quarterly, semi-annually, or annually). Top-up premiums are also available to maximize your account value.

If you'd like more specific details, such as premium amounts, rider terms, or coverage limits, feel free to ask! You might also want to inquire about the differences between the Increasing and Level Cover options or how the auto-extension feature works.
